
# Tests

## Two-lamp hardware integration test

Connect exactly two ESP32-C3 GlowLight lamps via USB and run:

```bash
make test-integration
```

The runner detects both `/dev/ttyACM*` devices, flashes the
`esp32c3-integration` profile, and verifies:

- mutual ESP-NOW discovery occurs exactly once
- mode changes propagate to the peer
- option changes propagate to the peer
- heartbeats do not create phantom nodes, crashes, or reboots

Use already flashed integration firmware with explicit ports:

```bash
python3 test/hil/two_lamp_sync.py --skip-flash --ports /dev/ttyACM0 /dev/ttyACM1
```
